<p>Iranian Parliament Speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf, who has led Tehran&#x27;s negotiations with the United States, has been appointed special representative for China affairs, Iran&#x27;s semi-official Tasnim news agency reported on May 17, citing informed sources. Tasnim said President Masoud Pezeshkian proposed the appointment and Supreme Leader Ayatollah Mojtaba Khamenei approved it. The role gives Ghalibaf responsibility for Iran-China relations across fields and for coordination among national bodies handling China-related matters, according to Tasnim&#x27;s account. The report did not say whether he would remain parliament speaker.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/qG0oTgItWhvSrgzVv-xvzovAmaWzrqkoEvOv7ospW2aJ7NAl_DKV0Sx4Hx9QojM3HpnnMJRaBG8fnPWYT3ZIicyDD75UsydmZ3MPJXKfabs1UDEx8M9kCVAt2mvFqWKPGpWIlTRp' alt='Iranian Parliament Speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf, appointed special representative for China affairs.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Timing: CNA&#x27;s Taipei report linked the appointment to the period after the Trump-Xi meeting, where Iran-related issues were discussed.</li><li>Past roles: Ghalibaf served as an Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps commander and mayor of Tehran before becoming parliament speaker.</li><li>Elite channel: CNA reported that during the US-Iran war, Ghalibaf had been viewed as an important link among Iran&#x27;s political, security and religious elites.</li><li>Source variation: CNA&#x27;s first wire said it was unclear who made the appointment, while other accounts attributed the proposal and approval to Pezeshkian and Khamenei.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Tasnim News Agency&#x27;s informed sources: The sources said the nature of Ghalibaf&#x27;s appointment gave his mandate a different level of authority from previous representatives. (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260517-iranian-parliament-speaker-appointed-as-special-envoy-to-china-report/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li><li>White House: After the Trump-Xi meeting, the White House said both sides agreed the Strait of Hormuz must remain open and Iran cannot have nuclear weapons; CNA also reported that the readout said Xi opposed militarization of the strait and any transit fees there. (<a href='https://www.cna.com.tw/news/acn/202605170188.aspx'>Central News Agency</a>)</li><li>China&#x27;s Xinhua News Agency: Xinhua&#x27;s account said President Trump and Xi exchanged views on the Middle East and other major international and regional issues, without listing the specific points cited by Washington. (<a href='https://www.cna.com.tw/news/acn/202605170188.aspx'>Central News Agency</a>)</li><li>Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf: CNA reported that Ghalibaf warned on X on May 12 that any US approach other than accepting Iran&#x27;s stated rights would fail and cost US taxpayers more over time. (<a href='https://www.cna.com.tw/news/acn/202605170188.aspx'>Central News Agency</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-chief-negotiator-ghalibaf-appointed-to-oversee-ties-with-china-media'>Iran chief negotiator Ghalibaf appointed to oversee ties with China: Media</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-chief-negotiator-ghalibaf-appointed-to-oversee-ties-with-china-media/article70991197.ece'>Iran chief negotiator Ghalibaf appointed to oversee ties with China: media</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://news.ltn.com.tw/news/world/breakingnews/5440215'>「靠中」來「喬」美伊和談？ 伊朗國會議長兼首席談判代表出任中國事務特別代表</a> - ltn.com.tw</li><li><a href='https://www.cna.com.tw/news/aopl/202605170189.aspx'>伊朗媒體：國會議長卡利巴夫獲任命　負責對中關係</a> - cna.com.tw</li><li><a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260517-iranian-parliament-speaker-appointed-as-special-envoy-to-china-report/'>Iranian parliament speaker appointed as special envoy to China: Report</a> - middleeastmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.khan.co.kr/article/202605172210001/'>이란 ‘대미 협상